<title>UK: UK's Brown cuts corporation tax by 2 pct points.</title>
<headline>UK's Brown cuts corporation tax by 2 pct points.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK Chancellor Gordon Brown said on Wednesday that he would cut the main rate of corporation tax by two percentage points to 31 percent.</p>
<p>The cut will start from April 1997, he said, adding that this was to help companies make long-term decisions and make the UK &quot;the obvious first choice for new investment.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
